# Chart Visualization Skill

When a task involves designing, refining, critiquing, or choosing a chart, graph, analytical dashboard panel, report visualization, or other data-display surface, use the global `tufte-viz` skill at `/Users/admin/.codex/skills/tufte-viz/SKILL.md`.

Reach for `tufte-viz` especially when the work includes:

- picking the right chart form for a comparison or trend
- simplifying an existing visualization
- improving clarity, hierarchy, or graphical honesty
- reducing chartjunk or redundant labels
- planning small multiples, sparklines, or dense analytical displays
- reviewing whether a dashboard/chart is misleading or visually noisy

Keep using project-specific rules in `.cursor/rules/` for implementation details after the visualization direction is set.
